From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
Date: Sat Oct 31 12:30:00 2026 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: cix: sky1: fix pcie_x2_rc rcsu strap/status addresses

The pcie_x2_rc node's "rcsu_strap" and "rcsu_status" reg entries use
0x0a0600340 and 0x0a0600440 -- an extra hex digit compared with the
0x0a060340/0x0a060440 used by the rest of the CIX register map and
with the MS-R1 firmware's CIXH2020 PRC _CRS (0x0a060340/0x0a060440).

The addresses are only consumed on DT boots (the MS-R1 boots ACPI and
the vendor driver gets these windows from ACPI), but they are plainly
wrong and would move the x2 controller's strap/status window into an
unmapped area on a DT system.

Same fix as Armbian's uefi-arm64-dt-7.3/1001-sky1-pcie-x2-fix.patch.

Signed-off-by: grimtickle-overlay <overlay@localhost>
---
 0183-arm64-dts-cix-fix-sky1-pcie-x2-rcsu-addresses.patch | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/cix/sky1.dtsi
@@ -661,8 +661,8 @@
 			compatible = "cix,sky1-pcie-host";
 			reg = <0x00 0x0a0c0000 0x00 0x10000>,
 			      <0x00 0x26000000 0x00 0x3000000>,
-			      <0x00 0x0a0600340 0x00 0x20>,
-			      <0x00 0x0a0600440 0x00 0x20>,
+			      <0x00 0x0a060340 0x00 0x20>,
+			      <0x00 0x0a060440 0x00 0x20>,
 			      <0x00 0x40000000 0x00 0x00100000>;
 			reg-names = "reg", "cfg", "rcsu_strap", "rcsu_status", "msg";
 			ranges = <0x01000000 0x0 0x40100000 0x0 0x40100000 0x0 0x00100000>,
